<title>UK: BA Q3 pretax profit up 8.7 pct.</title>
<headline>BA Q3 pretax profit up 8.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>				(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.2		    vs 9.1</p>
<p> Operating profit	 131		    vs 152</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    113		    vs 104</p>
<p> Turnover		   2,016		  vs 1,895</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British airline is British Airways Plc. The company said the strength of sterling forced yields, the amount received per kilometre flow down by 1.8 percent.</p>
<p>				    - Nine months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		48.9		   vs 42.9</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    583		    vs 534</p>
<p> Turnover		   6,410		  vs 5,924</p>
<p>Mainline scheduled services</p>
<p>				 - Three months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p> Overall load factor    69.7 pct	     vs 69.4 pct</p>
<p> Passenger load factor  71.2 pct	     vs 70.8 pct</p>
<p> Passengers (million)   8.034		  vs 7.607</p>
<p> Cargo (tonnes)	   183,000		vs 179,000</p>
<p> Passenger revenue</p>
<p> per RPK		   6.44p		  vs 6.56p</p>
<p> Cargo revenue</p>
<p> per CTK		   15.06p		 vs 16.04p</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
